pressed  in one way or another  in episode 5 Thomas explains that man is  created in two parts ourselves and a  shadow normally these two parts live  peacefully side-by-side but sometimes  one tries to overpower the other which  causes it's a victim to hear the bells  of the church tower these copies will  stop at nothing to fully take over their  subjects lives to bring balance to  whomever's life they've come for for  example Lucas is depicted as a wimp he's  constantly bullied and doesn't even have  the courage to defeat his clone when it  attacks the clone however is a badass  who takes matters into his own hands and  isn't afraid to get his hands dirty  each of these clones are trying to fix  something missing from their copies  lives even if that means killing to do  so as we later find out these copies can  be killed but they simply reemerge from  the lake brand-new if that happens this  is why Thomas kept the clone copy of an  ax in his attic for 17 years he knew  this copy if left unattended would  search relentlessly for the real Annie  if he didn't do something so he kept it  chained away the perfect encapsulation  of this is the wolf Thomas has chained  outside his hotel he thinks these copies  can be quote domesticated and as we  learn through the character of Albert  yes these clones can completely take  over the lives of their victims as a  teen Albert was in love with Anna but  Anna wanted to be free leave Kieran and  move away  she even cheated on him with a man will  later find his petrol she says she's  pregnant and that Albert is not the  father but what if Anna was lying about  this what if Albert was the real father  I actually thought this would tie into a  huge reveal at the end of the season but  that didn't happen  that would mean that Daria and Mauro are  Albert's kids making them half siblings  with Mickey and Giulio and if you've  seen the entire season that would mean  Daria and Giulio hooking up would mean  some serious incest after getting dumped  a young Clara takes Albert out on the  lake to console him she's in love with  him but Albert's heart belongs to  Annagh suddenly albert is attacked by  his copy resulting in his death and the  new albert takes over a copy who doesn't  care if he makes it with clara something  the real albert would never have done  eventually they'll marry and have two  kids Micky and Giulio Clara keeps it a  secret because she finally gets what she  always wanted to be with Albert even if  it's all a lie  later in the season when Clara is  confronted by a copy of herself she  doesn't fight it  she knows her life has been one big lie  her romance with Albert was never real  she'd rather be dead than live with this  lie onward to the beginning of the last  episode titled the maze this is a  reference to the series of tunnels and  bunkers constructed by the Italians  during World War two in the event of an  invasion the characters often refer to  it affectionately as the plains of the  dead the real Anna has been held captive  by her copy and conveniently there's a  piece of wire she uses to escape in an  ironic twist Tomas last episode was held  captive in the same attic he held Anna's  copy and he's put in there with the wolf  he's able to fight it off and sets it  free the kids who are composed of Daria  maro Miki and Giulio travel up the  mountain in search of their parents  Thomas and clone Clara team up as well  in search of the kids who they know will  be in danger from Albert and Albert is  continuing his love affair with Anna  what these two don't realize yet is  their love is a lie to the real Albert  fell in love with the real Anna but  these two are both copies they're not  the same people this will come into play  a bit later meanwhile the kids find the  entrance to the tunnels and uncover a  pile of Bones they believe it could  belong to Italian soldiers who were  defending the tunnels but as we learn  the Nazis never ended up invading so why  are there dead bodies it's almost as if  the writers were like hey wouldn't it be  cool if they stumbled upon some bones  but they never explain it well coming up  the side of the mountain Thomas and  Clara uncover the bodies of Lucas and  Berger who were killed last episode  burger was Thomas's best and only real  friend and Kieran and this Lucas was the  evil clone of the real one which begs  the question can a clone come back if  its original has already been killed  this is never really explored in the  show but  I think not a copy can't be created  without an original so Lucas is now  likely gone for good  the Albert and Anna clones find out that  the real Anna has escaped remember how I  said that their love is a lie since  they're both clones well here is where  we learn why the Anna clone wanted to  kill the original right away but at the  orders of Albert had held her captive in  the tunnels so she would starve Anna  accuses Albert that this was his plan  all along that he never wanted to kill  Anna because that's the real woman he  fell in love with clone Anna bashes her  head into the wall in an attempt to  trick the kids into thinking she was the  one held captive and the kids aren't  really dumb and gets split up in the  creepy World War two tunnels where they  just saw a bunch of human bones Daria  and Morrel finally to Anna's separately  but then the question remains who is the  real Anna and this is where this series  goes extremely dark so dark in fact that  this has to be one of the saddest most  tragic endings I've ever seen in the  seasons climax Daria and Morrel have to  figure out which of their mothers is the  real one and to make matters worse  Albert appears aiming his gun Albert has  realized that neither one of the Anna's  are his Anna the clone Anna is simply  that a clone and the real Anna he never  fell in love with because he's a clone  himself it was the original version of  him that fell in love with that Anna the  two and his fight each other and Albert  ends up shooting both of them and to  make things even more twisted he shoots  himself in front of his own kids so  right off the bat we have a double  murder-suicide in front of some kids but  it gets even worse  one of the Anna's survives and escapes  as we'll find out this is Anna's clone  but her escape is short-lived as Mauro  tracks her down and holds her at  gunpoint she tries to explain herself  that the real Anna was weak and couldn't  protect them from their abusive father  earlier in the season we learned that  Mauro's hearing loss was caused by his  father when he pushed young Mauro  causing him to bonk his head and lose  part of his hearing and his clone was  simply a protector that's why she killed  their father in cold blood  Anna ends up falling over the edge of  the cliff plummeting to her death as her  family watches on and that's just part  of what makes this ending so dark first  we have Daria and Mauro lose both of  their parents even witnessing the death  of their mother  in person Miki and Giulio watches their  father murders the Anna's then takes his  own life in front of them Clara later  shows them the grave of the real Albert  and the kids find out that their father  was one of these evil copies their  entire life not to mention their real  mother is dead and they're left with  this copy of their mom if that isn't  enough a character by the name of Ober  brings Lucas's dead body to his father  'über isn't given much screen time  throughout the season but he's part of  this rival family that once held control  over Kieran but when Kieran was part of  Austria his family held sway so he's got  some personal vendetta against the  Terrenas  he says that the lake has awoken once  again and that the Reynes must be  destroyed Mickey and Aria start to hear  the sounds of the bell tower meaning  copies of themselves are on their way  but since the lake is frozen the copies  are trapped even though their copies  it's still terrifying to watch as they  pound on the ice gasping for air but if  there's a season two it's most likely  that these copies will find their way  out from the frozen lake Curran is a  deeply tragic series with almost all of  its characters losing the most important  people in their lives even Thomas loses  his best friend and daughter but more  tragic is that I personally didn't feel  connected to any of the characters and  at times the writing feels contrived and  forced in order to make the plot work  most of the twists are predictable in  the show and there weren't any major  holy [ __ ] moments that define many of  these types of shows but if you're  desperate to have something to tide you  over until the new season of dark comes  out give this one a try thank you for  watching and if you haven't done so  already please make sure to LIKE and  subscribe and for more bat takes you can  follow me on twitter at big story whitey  until next time remember daddy loves you  very much
 

